SLLM patch 11 (phase2-prefill2): kernel_sllm_pfa2, a faster prefill attention kernel with the per-row arithmetic of
patch 7's kernel_sllm_pfa (so still bitwise ggml's kernel_flash_attn_ext_tensor), and a stream form of the op.
- Two consecutive visible 64-cell blocks share one Q K^T matmul2d run over 128 cells and, when no row rescales in
  the second block, one P V run over 128 cells (matmul2d's output does not depend on how its K extent is split into
  runs); O is rescaled only when some row of the threadgroup moved its running max.
- Streams: a hinted FLASH_ATTN_EXT with ne3 = S > 1 (q, k, v, dst; k / v may share one view with nb3 = 0, the mask
  per stream or shared) runs as one dispatch, stream s writing dst rows s*T .. (sllm-core puts several equal-size
  prefill chunks of one step in one op this way, so their outputs need no concat). Only kernel_sllm_pfa2 takes S > 1.
kernels/prefill.metal: the kernel (D 128/256, G 2/4), stream offsets in it and in kernel_sllm_pfa_q, args field pad0
renamed ns and five stream strides appended (same layout in ggml-metal-pfa.h). ggml-metal-pfa.m: SLLM_PFA_PAIR
(default on; 0 = patch 7's kernel, one stream only), threadgroup memory, stream checks / plan / scratch / dispatch,
status field "kernel", a fifth self-test case (long shared prefix, a hidden block that shifts the pairing) and a
stream self-test (3 streams sharing K/V, different masks: bitwise the one-stream results).
Against llama.cpp b11669 (source tarball 620d222) after patches 0001..0010, applied with patch -p1 in ggml/.

